S.append(P("Why these numbers", h2)); S.append(rule())
S.append(bullets(["<b>Regeneration 30, back at 30.</b> In Badrick, Alucard puts a .454 Casull through his skull and he stands up a few seconds later; Alucard then cuts him to ribbons and he walks away. Thirty a turn is a troll's regeneration tripled, and the stand-up with no death saves is the scene. The radiant and fire clause is the Jackal: a gun built, in the story, to kill a Regenerator, firing blessed exploding shells; in 5e that is a damage type that stops the regrowth for a turn, and the only way an ordinary fighter ever ends him is to keep that pressure up until the heart.",
 "<b>The bayonets.</b> He throws a dozen at a time and never runs out; in 5e that is a dagger that is always in his hand, Nick for the third throw, and a cone for the fan. The +2d6 against undead is why a vampire with a thousand lives bleeds from them and a human does not.",
 "<b>The pages.</b> The wall that Alucard cannot cross and the cage he once sealed a vampire in are Channel Divinity, which is the Paladin's own resource for exactly this; the vanish is Misty Step. None of it needs a new system.",
 "<b>The Nail.</b> Regeneration 60, thorns that burn everything within ten feet, and the grapple that pierced Alucard's heart. It is not sized to the arena; it is sized to a creature with Level 0 released, which is the only thing he ever used it on. The exit clause (0 hit points, the Nail torn out, 40 damage breaks it) is the manga: Seras's shadow and Alucard's hand."]))
S.append(P("Build, level by level", h2)); S.append(rule())
S.append(P("Point buy 12 / 14 / 14 / 8 / 12 / 13, Acolyte +2 Cha, +1 Wis; the Regenerator then sets Strength 20, Dexterity 20 and Constitution 22, so the feats go to Charisma and Wisdom. His history before Iscariot is thin in the manga; the early levels follow what it gives.", small))
