def snap(name, where, lvl, lines, checked):
    content = [P(name, snapname), P(where + "  ·  " + lvl, stattag)] + [P(l, snapline) for l in lines] + [P("<b>The feat, checked.</b> " + checked, snapline)]
    t = Table([[content]], colWidths=[W]); t.setStyle(TableStyle([("BACKGROUND",(0,0),(-1,-1),PARCH),("LINEBEFORE",(0,0),(0,-1),2.5,GREEN),("LEFTPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),10),("RIGHTPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),10),("TOPPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),7),("BOTTOMPADDING",(0,0),(-1,-1),7)]))
    return KeepTogether([t, Spacer(1,7)])
S.append(snap("Iscariot's Paladin", "before the manga · the priest, the surgery, the years of vampires", "Levels 1–8 · Paladin 1–8", ["Str 20, Dex 20, Con 22 from level 4 · <b>AC</b> 17 · <b>HP</b> up to 128 · bayonets +9, three a turn from level 5 · Divine Smite · Regeneration 30 · Aura of Protection"], "A vampire is a CR 13 with Regeneration 20 and a weakness to radiant; a level-6 Anderson throws three blessed bayonets a turn for 1d6+5 plus 2d6 radiant each and a 3d8 smite, and nothing it does to him stays done. The manga says he never lost one. The sheet says that is the correct result of 130 damage a round against a thing with 144 hit points that cannot close a holy wound."))
S.append(snap("Badrick", "Hellsing Ultimate I · Alucard and Seras in a hospital", "Levels 9–10 · Paladin 9–10", ["<b>HP</b> 150 · Haste · Aura of Courage · Vow of Enmity on Alucard"], "Alucard is a CR 30 vampire with lives to spend and Regeneration 50. Anderson pins him with a fan of bayonets (Dex DC 18, and Alucard does not dodge), takes the head off with a Vow of Enmity crit, and Alucard puts a .454 Casull through his skull: a crit for 60-odd, and a Regenerator at 150 hit points stands up at the start of his next turn. The cuts that follow, dozens of them, never reach 20 radiant in a round, so nothing stops the regrowth. The fight ends because Integra arrives and Maxwell calls him home: two walls of pages and a storm of paper, which is Channel Divinity and Misty Step. Neither of them could kill the other, and the sheet agrees."))
S.append(snap("London", "Hellsing Ultimate VII–VIII · the Ninth Crusade, Level 0, the river of the dead", "Levels 13–19 · Paladin 13–19", ["<b>HP</b> up to 270 · Banishment, Hold Monster, Destructive Wave · Soul of Vengeance · Radiant Strikes · Tough"], "Alucard's familiars are thousands of undead between CR 1 and CR 10, and he walks through them. Bayonet Storm is 6d6+2d6 radiant to everything in a cone, Destructive Wave is 5d6 radiant in thirty feet, the Wall of Pages makes them wait their turn, and Radiant Strikes means every bayonet he throws is a wound that does not heal. He breaks Maxwell's barrier with one bayonet (an object with AC 15 and 30 hit points) and lets the crusade die for being a crusade. Then he reaches the one he came for."))
S.append(snap("The Nail", "Hellsing Ultimate VIII · Alucard at Level 0, and then a human", "Level 20 · Paladin 20", ["The headline block, and then the Monster of God: Regeneration 60, thorns, reach, the grapple"], "Alucard with Level 0 released is a CR 35 with every life he has ever taken; as a man, Anderson cannot win, and the sheet knows it: 74 a round against a thing with thousands of hit points and Regeneration 50 is a draw that lasts until he is tired. So the Nail. Holy Thorns burn 4d8 radiant a turn into every undead within ten feet, which is the familiars dying by the hundred; the thorn vines reach fifteen feet and grapple, which is the one that goes through Alucard's heart. He cannot be killed with the Nail in him. Then Seras's shadow pins him, Alucard's hand goes through his chest, and the Nail comes out at DC 25 against a Strength of 30. He dies as what he wanted to be, and asks to be remembered as it."))
